# Do not run dependency lifecycle scripts (preinstall/install/postinstall).
#
# Supply-chain defence: a compromised transitive dependency's install script is
# arbitrary code executing with the full environment of whoever runs `npm ci` —
# on a developer laptop that means SSH keys, ~/.aws, and shell history; in CI it
# means every secret exported into the job. Recent npm worm campaigns
# (chalk/debug, Shai-Hulud) all propagated through exactly this hook. Disabling
# it costs us nothing here: no direct or transitive dependency in this tree
# needs an install script to produce a working build. Verified from a clean
# node_modules — `npm ci`, `npm run lint`, `tsc --noEmit` and `npm test` all
# pass with scripts off, and the four packages that do declare one
# (@google/genai, esbuild, protobufjs, unrs-resolver) are each fine without it:
# esbuild and unrs-resolver resolve their native binaries at require time, and
# @google/genai's is a literal no-op echo.
#
# If a future dependency genuinely needs one, do NOT delete this line — allow
# that single package instead, e.g.:
#   npm rebuild <package>       # one-off, in the step that needs it
ignore-scripts=true
